1. Definitions and scope
1.1 In this licence:
(a) "we", "us" and "our" mean MarketAI;
(b) "you" means the natural or legal person who holds the MarketAI account whose bots
    the connector follows. Anyone who installs, configures or runs the connector for
    that person does so on that person's behalf (section 4.3);
(c) "consumer" means a natural person acting for purposes outside their trade,
    business, craft or profession, or any other person whom the law applicable to you
    treats as a consumer;
(d) "the connector" means the MarketAI Connector software in every form: the container
    image ghcr.io/sergimes/marketai-connector, every copy, version and update of it,
    and the source code it contains;
(e) "the repository" means the public repository sergimes/marketai-connector;
(f) "MarketAI's service" means the service offered at app.marketai.trade, including its
    signal feeds and the My bots page;
(g) "order" means any instruction the connector sends to an exchange to open, change or
    close a position, or to place, change or cancel an instruction resting at the
    exchange, such as a stop-loss or a take-profit;
(h) "exchange" means the trading platform, such as Bitget or Hyperliquid, that holds an
    account the connector trades;
(i) "failure" means any error, defect, malfunction or interruption of the connector or
    of MarketAI's service, including an order that your bots' signals did not call for,
    an order sent with a wrong size, and an order that was not sent, changed or
    cancelled when it should have been.
1.2 Section 2 sets out what anyone may do with the repository's files. Sections 3 to 7
apply to the connector. The other sections apply to the connector and, when you use
them with the connector, to the repository's files.

