7. Updates, term and termination
7.1 The connector updates itself unless you turn automatic updates off. Every update is
subject to this licence. We change the connector only for a valid reason: to fix an
error; for security; to adapt it to a change in the law, in an exchange's systems or
rules, or in MarketAI's service; or to improve how it follows your bots' signals. The
release notes describe what each version changes. If you are a consumer and a change
would harm your use of the connector in more than a minor way, we will tell you by
email, in advance, what changes and when, and you may then end your subscription free
of charge as the law provides.
7.2 This licence ends automatically when you no longer hold a MarketAI account with at
least one bot. We may also end it by notice if you breach it and do not remedy the
breach within 14 days of that notice, or at once if the breach cannot be remedied, such
as a breach of section 4.4.
7.3 We may end this licence for all users, or stop offering the connector, by giving at
least 30 days' notice. If you are a consumer, you will then be refunded what you paid
us for any period you can no longer use.
7.4 When this licence ends, you must stop running the connector and delete your copies
of it. Stopping the connector does not close your positions (see DISCLAIMER.md).

8. Orders placed by the connector
8.1 Once you start the connector, it places, changes and cancels orders on your
exchange account automatically, without asking you each time, in order to follow your
bots' signals and their state on My bots and to protect your positions, as described in
DISCLAIMER.md. By starting it, you authorise it to do so. You decide whether it runs,
with which bots, on which account and at what leverage, and you may pause or stop it at
any time.
8.2 Every order the connector sends while it runs for you is sent in your name and with
your API keys, whatever caused it. It is your order: it binds you towards your exchange
and any third party, and its results, gains and losses alike, are yours. This includes
the risks described in DISCLAIMER.md, such as a stop-loss filled at a worse price than
its trigger price, a take-profit that is not filled, a signal missed while your
computer was off or asleep, and the closes described in section 8.3. Whether, and to
what extent, we must compensate you for a loss that a failure caused is governed only
by section 10.
8.3 The connector closes every open position of a bot, at market if a limit order does
not fill, when the bot is paused, is waiting for MarketAI's approval, is not paid, or
its signal feed is withdrawn; when MarketAI's service reports a state for the bot that
the connector does not recognise; and, for the positions of the old signal feed, when
you switch the bot to another signal feed. Such a close can lock in a loss.
8.4 You must check your exchange account regularly. If you notice an order you did not
expect, you must stop the connector without delay and inform us through
app.marketai.trade.

