9.1 The connector has no price of its own: it is supplied with your MarketAI bots.
Subject to section 9.2, it is provided as it is and as available, and we give no
warranty of any kind, express or implied, including as to its quality, fitness for a
particular purpose, accuracy, availability or results. We do not warrant that it is
free of errors, that it runs without interruption, or that every order will be placed,
filled, changed or cancelled as intended.
9.2 If you are a consumer, section 9.1 does not affect the rights the law gives you,
including, where the law gives them, the right to a connector that conforms to the
contract and receives the updates needed to keep it so. If you do not install an update
that we made available and told you about, together with what not installing it would
mean, we are not liable for a lack of conformity that that update alone would have
remedied, unless you could not install it because our installation instructions were
inadequate.

10. Liability
10.1 Trading leveraged derivatives carries a high risk of loss, and you do so at your
own risk. We do not promise or guarantee that following any signal feed will make a
profit. A signal feed may lose money even when everything works as intended, and such
losses are yours.
10.2 We are not liable for any loss or damage arising from the following, except to
the extent that a failure caused it (sections 10.3 and 10.4 govern that):
(a) movements in market prices;
(b) orders the connector sends in accordance with your bots' signals and their state on
    My bots, and the results of such orders;
(c) your exchange, your computer, your internet connection, or any other system or
    service outside our control;
(d) the settings you choose, or the safekeeping of your API keys;
(e) signals that were not received or acted upon while the connector was not running
    or not connected.
10.3 If you use the connector in the course of a trade, business or profession, we are
not liable to you for any loss or damage caused by a failure, nor for any loss of
profit, loss of opportunity, or indirect or consequential loss, whatever its cause.
10.4 If you are a consumer, our liability to you for loss or damage caused by a failure
is the liability the law provides. Under that law:
(a) we are liable only for loss that is a necessary consequence of the failure and
    that was foreseen, or could have been foreseen, when you accepted this licence;
(b) we are not liable for loss that you could reasonably have avoided or reduced once
    you noticed the failure, or should reasonably have noticed it, for example by
    stopping the connector as section 8.4 asks, nor for loss that an update would have
    avoided in the case described in section 9.2;
(c) our liability is reduced to the extent that your own acts or omissions contributed
    to the loss;
(d) we are not liable for loss caused by events that could not have been foreseen or
    that, if foreseen, could not have been avoided.
10.5 Nothing in this licence excludes or limits liability for wilful misconduct or gross
negligence, for death or personal injury, or any other liability that cannot be
excluded or limited under applicable law, including product liability law.
10.6 If we disagree as to whether a failure caused an order or a loss, the burden of
proof is as provided by law, and this licence does not alter it. If you are a consumer
and claim that the connector did not conform, you must cooperate with us, as far as
reasonably possible and necessary and by the least intrusive means available, to
establish whether the cause lay in your own computer, network or settings, for example
by sending us the logs of the bot concerned. If you do not, and to the extent that the
law so allows, the burden of proving that the connector did not conform is on you.
10.7 If you use the connector in the course of a trade, business or profession, you
will compensate us for any claim that a third party brings against us because you
breached section 4.4 or 5.

11. Third-party software
The image contains open-source software by other authors, including Python, Debian
packages and Python libraries. Each component is licensed under its own terms and not
under this licence, and its licence text is included in the image. The list of those
components, and where to obtain their source code, is in
/usr/share/doc/marketai-connector/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES in the image. The updater that
compose.yml runs (watchtower) is a separate program under its own licence.

12. The MarketAI name
"MarketAI" is our name. This licence grants no right to use it, except to state
truthfully that you use the connector.

13. Amendments
13.1 We may amend this licence only for one of these reasons: a change in the law; a
change in an exchange's rules or systems; a change in MarketAI's service that requires
it; a security need; or to make its wording clearer.
13.2 We will notify you by email at least 30 days before an amendment takes effect.
Versions of the connector released from then on also report it in their logs and ask
you, in the setup, to accept the amended licence.
13.3 From the day an amendment takes effect, your bots open no new positions until you
have accepted it, and we may refuse versions of the connector released before it. If
you do not accept an amendment, you may terminate your MarketAI subscription; if you
are a consumer, you will then be refunded what you paid us for any period you can no
longer use.
13.4 An amendment that is solely in your favour, such as a translation of this licence,
may take effect immediately and does not need to be accepted again.

